test interpret
test run
target scry32

; The absolute value of an unsigned-tagged input (a `uext` parameter)
; consumed by a signed operation. `iabs(INT_MIN)` wraps to `INT_MIN`
; (0x80000000), which the arithmetic shift must treat as negative, yielding
; 0xC0000000; a logical shift would yield 0x40000000. The other inputs
; exercise the negation path with a positive result and the pass-through
; path.

function %iabs_sshr(i32 uext) -> i32 uext {
block0(v0: i32):
    v1 = iabs v0
    v2 = iconst.i32 1
    v3 = sshr v1, v2
    return v3
}
; run: %iabs_sshr(-2147483648) == -1073741824
; run: %iabs_sshr(-5) == 2
; run: %iabs_sshr(7) == 3
